{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/838159-werewolves-and-obfuscate","id":838159,"title":"Werewolves and Obfuscate","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-02-27T12:05:45-08:00","id":838159,"title":"Werewolves and Obfuscate","content":"How do you work Obfuscate when used against werewolves in your chronicle? For tracking an Obfuscated target if the gift Impossible Spoor is used then I'm thinking a Clash of Wills of Wisdom + Primal Urge versus Obfuscate + Blood Potency to allow tracking to take place but this wouldn't necessarily allow detection. For actually piercing though Obfuscate I'm thinking either<br /> a) Honed Senses to attempt a Clash of Wills and then Cunning + Primal Urge versus Obfuscate + Blood Potency; or<br /> b) saying wolf exceptional senses alone (possibly not human, just wolf) allow for a chance with the Clash of Wills being Auspice Renown + Primal Urge versus Obfuscate + Blood Potency<br /> <br /> As well, for Scent the Unnatural I'm thinking a Clash of Wills here using Purity would allow for the Uratha to know something unnatural but unseen was present if the Gift was used. How do all of you run it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4586-vedic","name":"Vedic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-27T12:20:07-08:00","id":838167,"title":"","content":"Impossible Spoor is a definitely Clash of Wills for me. As is Scent the Unnatural. Honed Senses I'd rule no. I would also allow Hunter's Aspect to break Obfuscate if the werewolf has managed to somehow perceive the Vampire through some other means.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-27T13:45:01-08:00","id":838205,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vedic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/838159-werewolves-and-obfuscate#post838159\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How do you work Obfuscate when used against werewolves in your chronicle? For tracking an Obfuscated target if the gift Impossible Spoor is used then I'm thinking a Clash of Wills of Wisdom + Primal Urge versus Obfuscate + Blood Potency to allow tracking to take place but this wouldn't necessarily allow detection. For actually piercing though Obfuscate I'm thinking either<br /> a) Honed Senses to attempt a Clash of Wills and then Cunning + Primal Urge versus Obfuscate + Blood Potency; or<br /> b) saying wolf exceptional senses alone (possibly not human, just wolf) allow for a chance with the Clash of Wills being Auspice Renown + Primal Urge versus Obfuscate + Blood Potency<br /> <br /> As well, for Scent the Unnatural I'm thinking a Clash of Wills here using Purity would allow for the Uratha to know something unnatural but unseen was present if the Gift was used. How do all of you run it?</div> </div> </div> </div>A werewolf's Clash of Wills is done with their auspice renown, regardless of what the dice pool to the gift is.<br /> <br /> And yes, the whole deal of Primal Urge, the ability to perceive otherworldly things with hyper honed senses, to the point you can sniff out the platonic ideal of say, death, would allow for them to contest Obfuscate with their base heightened senses in my games. YMMV.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-27T14:02:28-08:00","id":838210,"title":"","content":"Werewolves only use Auspice renown for things regarding their template or anything else that doesn't have a renown of it sown. Shadow gifts and others relying on Renown use the appropriate renown for the facet.<br /> <br /> Regardless, as to the original question, I'd say that as mentioned scent of the unnatural and Impossible spoor would allow a Clash. Honed senses and basic werewolf senses wouldn't, though, in my opinion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-27T14:03:14-08:00","id":838211,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/838159-werewolves-and-obfuscate?p=838205#post838205\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A werewolf's Clash of Wills is done with their auspice renown, regardless of what the dice pool to the gift is.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not quite.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The players of all characters using conflicting powers enter a contested roll-off, each using a pool of her Primal Urge plus her dots in the Renown associated with the Facet she is using or her auspice Renown for other abilities. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-27T14:09:39-08:00","id":838215,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/838159-werewolves-and-obfuscate?p=838205#post838205\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And yes, the whole deal of Primal Urge, the ability to perceive otherworldly things with hyper honed senses, to the point you can sniff out the platonic ideal of say, death, would allow for them to contest Obfuscate with their base heightened senses in my games. YMMV.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Obfuscate makes you ignore them, it doesn't actually make them invisible or hide them. I wouldn't think scent would cue it off so easily as it literally hides from all senses and even makes you ignore them. I'd say they would need a reason to begin looking (context clues like it says specifically in the discipline). Obfuscate is a mind influencing power, not a light bending or invisibility power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/460-rani-neferet","name":"Rani Neferet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar460_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"971"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-27T14:18:00-08:00","id":838220,"title":"","content":"I don't think Obfuscate does anything to stop tracking at all; you wouldn't need Impossible Spoor to track an Obfuscated vampire.<br /> <br /> Scent the Unnatural would\u200b Clash of Wills vs Obfuscate for detecting where the vampire is. However, even if it failed, Scent the Unnatural could still detect the Obfuscate effect itself, effectively IDing the vampire's location except only revealing to the werewolf that there is a supernatural effect there, and nothing more.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-27T14:35:52-08:00","id":838228,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rani Neferet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/838159-werewolves-and-obfuscate?p=838215#post838215\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Obfuscate makes you ignore them, it doesn't actually make them invisible or hide them. I wouldn't think scent would cue it off so easily as it literally hides from all senses and even makes you ignore them. I'd say they would need a reason to begin looking (context clues like it says specifically in the discipline). Obfuscate is a mind influencing power, not a light bending or invisibility power.</div> </div> </div> </div>And under which grounds does Auspex allows to contest it, then?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-27T14:41:05-08:00","id":838229,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/838159-werewolves-and-obfuscate?p=838228#post838228\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And under which grounds does Auspex allows to contest it, then?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because Obfuscate makes you ignore what you percieve with your senses. Auspex is extrasensory perception, therefore not one of the things Obfuscate makes you ignore.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-27T14:43:06-08:00","id":838230,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/838159-werewolves-and-obfuscate?p=838229#post838229\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because Obfuscate makes you ignore what you percieve with your senses. Auspex is extrasensory perception, therefore not one of the things Obfuscate makes you ignore.</div> </div> </div> </div>Primal Urge is described as such as well:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#231F20\"><span style=\"font-family:Goudy\">Your character\u2019s connection to his ancestral roots, to the world around him and to the spirit world is measured by his Primal Urge. <b>It suggests how far he is able </b><b>to transcend a mundane understanding of reality and </b><b>perceive other possibilities and realms.</b> <b>Characters with </b><b>high Primal Urge are in touch with the spirit world and </b><b>the ephemeral, perceiving things that other werewolves </b><b>cannot. </b>They master their Essence and are able to invoke various Gifts and perform impressive supernatural feats. Characters with low Primal Urge have little connection to other worlds and senses or have yet to hone that <b>awareness</b>, focusing primarily on the material. They have little facility with Essence, are able to perform only limited Gifts and must rely on the capabilities of their bodies.</span></span> </div> </div> </div>Nevermind the examples in which animals are unaffected by it. Namely because &quot;drawing attention to yourself&quot; is far easier to someone who can hear everything that's happening in a whole city block, than comparing it with a mere human.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":576,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","user":"Ephsy","date":". 02-27-2016, 05:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-27T14:56:58-08:00","id":838235,"title":"","content":"Obfuscate isn't a spiritual power (or involved in 'other realms' at all), though, so I'm not sure how being in touch with the spirit world suggest it lets you defeat mental concealing powers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-27T15:05:38-08:00","id":838238,"title":"","content":"Extrasensory implies beyond the senses. That a werewolf's senses allow them to percieve things that others cannot does not make them extrasensory, any more than a dog being able to hear things humans cannot is extrasensory perception.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-27T15:40:29-08:00","id":838250,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/838159-werewolves-and-obfuscate?p=838238#post838238\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Extrasensory implies beyond the senses. That a werewolf's senses allow them to percieve things that others cannot does not make them extrasensory, any more than a dog being able to hear things humans cannot is extrasensory perception.</div> </div> </div> </div>Still doesn't explains how a