r","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-28T08:59:38-08:00","id":838667,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/838159-werewolves-and-obfuscate?p=838663#post838663\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would a werewolf in Kuruth, then, be able to target vampires in Obfuscation as if they weren't using it at all?<br /> <br /> I'm still waiting for confirmation on animals being immune to it in second edition.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I always thought the animals being immune to obfuscate thing was dumb, and as far as I know there's nothing to support it in 2e.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-28T09:27:22-08:00","id":838675,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/838159-werewolves-and-obfuscate?p=838238#post838238\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Extrasensory implies beyond the senses. That a werewolf's senses allow them to percieve things that others cannot does not make them extrasensory, any more than a dog being able to hear things humans cannot is extrasensory perception.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Question: Wouldn't that technically mean that a Mage using Mage Sight to try to see the vampire wouldn't be able to see the vampire since by your definition, it's just another form of &quot;seeing&quot; and thus gets ignored?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-28T09:39:21-08:00","id":838681,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/838159-werewolves-and-obfuscate?p=838675#post838675\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Question: Wouldn't that technically mean that a Mage using Mage Sight to try to see the vampire wouldn't be able to see the vampire since by your definition, it's just another form of &amp;quot;seeing&amp;quot; and thus gets ignored?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, Mage Sight is pretty much the definition of extrasensory. Just because sight is in the name doesn't mean it's literally a function of the mage's ocular nerves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-28T11:40:02-08:00","id":838730,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/838159-werewolves-and-obfuscate?p=838667#post838667\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, I always thought the animals being immune to obfuscate thing was dumb, and as far as I know there's nothing to support it in 2e.</div> </div> </div> </div> Wasn't it a holdover from Masquerae in the first place?. Pretty sure it was eliminated. There's nothing remotely close to suggesting that animals are immune in 2e, and even in 1e, it wasn't a given. It was a potential plot hook that people abused and assumed that having hellhounds were flawlessly going to see past Obfuscate all the time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-29T01:37:50-08:00","id":839024,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/838159-werewolves-and-obfuscate?p=838646#post838646\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not the presence of instincts that's important, it's the lack of higher order thinking.</div> </div> </div> </div>Where's that distinction mentioned?<br /> <br /> What makes lack of higher thought more verosimil than actually noticing a vampire under the clause of it calling your attention like it would with loudly stepping on a floor behind you? Not much.<br /> <br /> What makes lack of higher thought somehow extrasensory, as you've put it? Nothing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":576,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","user":"Ephsy","date":". 02-29-2016, 04:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-29T01:41:46-08:00","id":839025,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/838159-werewolves-and-obfuscate?p=838730#post838730\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Wasn't it a holdover from Masquerae in the first place?. Pretty sure it was eliminated. There's nothing remotely close to suggesting that animals are immune in 2e, and even in 1e, it wasn't a given. It was a potential plot hook that people abused and assumed that having hellhounds were flawlessly going to see past Obfuscate all the time.</div> </div> </div> </div>2e got only one book. One book, in which the description to attributes is like 2 sentences long. Excuse it for not including all the usual the info later supplements pointed at.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-29T06:57:23-08:00","id":839131,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/838159-werewolves-and-obfuscate?p=839025#post839025\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 2e got only one book. One book, in which the description to attributes is like 2 sentences long. Excuse it for not including all the usual the info later supplements pointed at.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Except that The Blood which you are using as a reference is almost totally invalidated by most of the changes, and even before a great deal of it was literally wrong, as in it had been written with a lot of Masquerade stuff in there that didn't match up with what was in Requiem in general. It was one of the worst books for anything but psychology. Rules-wise the Blood didn't know what game it was for except in about two locations, in which it made high blood potency vampires completely unplayable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/460-rani-neferet","name":"Rani Neferet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar460_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"971"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-29T07:09:49-08:00","id":839137,"title":"","content":"And... Nothing is going to supersede it until there's a publication alike. Personal opinions or not. It's what we've got to work with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-29T07:34:08-08:00","id":839158,"title":"","content":"Well, while the detection just using base senses may or may not work... how does this work for all of the Gift based sensory powers?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Also, since Obscufate is a mind hack power, the first dot anyways, wouldn't that mean stuff like Fearless Hunter might Clash it? Granted, the rules don't directly cause cause the Werewolf to sense since it's a &quot;defense&quot; against mental intrusions, but it's the idea being is that you're using a means to &quot;clear your mind&quot; of the psychic influence of the Vampire's obscufate, even though technically, that's not what the gift's fluff says.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-29T07:55:46-08:00","id":839174,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/838159-werewolves-and-obfuscate?p=839137#post839137\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And... Nothing is going to supersede it until there's a publication alike. Personal opinions or not. It's what we've got to work with.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Its not even valid, the only valid thing is Vtr 2e. That book is as thrown out as anything else. And even before that, supplements were all optional rules, not default. Your just wanting to cherry pick an old edition to justify your non-current interpretation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/460-rani-neferet","name":"Rani Neferet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar460_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"971"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-29T08:31:54-08:00","id":839199,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/838159-werewolves-and-obfuscate?p=839024#post839024\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Where's that distinction mentioned?</div> </div> </div> </div>You responded to MCN's post pointing out that the Blood also says mentally ill people can see through obfuscate by saying that werewolves have superior senses too. I was clarifying that superior senses has nothing to do with why the mentally ill can see through Obfuscate since, you know, they don't have superior senses.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/838159-werewolves-and-obfuscate?p=839024#post839024\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What makes lack of higher thought more verosimil than actually noticing a vampire under the clause of it calling your attention like it would with loudly stepping on a floor behind you? Not much.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because Obfuscate works by making observers ignore the sensory information they are receiving. It doesn't matter if you're receiving more detailed sensory information, Obfuscate still makes you ignore it. The vampire calling attention to itself breaks Obfuscate because if you're paying attention to the vampire you're not ignoring it any more. Also, stepping loudly is not an example of calling attention to yourself. The example is pulling a gun in a crowded place. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/838159-werewolves-and-obfuscate?p=839024#post839024\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What makes lack of higher thought somehow extrasensory, as you've put it? Nothing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right, nothing. Extrasensory perception is not the reason animals can see through Obfuscate in The Blood (which, again, was demonstrably wrong in several places, even in 1e). It says that animals (and mentally ill people) can see through it not because their senses are more powerful, but because their brains are too simple for Obfuscate to fool. Extrasensory perception allows you to pierce Obfuscate because you're perceiving the vampire with something other than the 5 senses, something that Obfuscate doesn't make you ignore. Two completely separate things.<br /> <br /> And, if all this still doesn't convince you, Requiem 2e pretty directly states that Obfuscate works on werewolves.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>page 137</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Obfuscate tricks the victim's mind directly, removing traces of the vampire from the sensory information reaching her brain, rather than fooling her senses directly. Obfuscate affects smell and taste as much as sight or hearing -<b> potentially useful if you've angered a pack of werewolves</b>, or a vampire with sharp Kindred senses.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-29T08:37:10-08:00","id":839202,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/838159-werewolves-and-obfuscate?p=839199#post839199\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You responded to MCN's post pointing out that the Blood also says mentally ill people can see through obfuscate by saying that werewolves have superior senses too. I was clarifying that superior senses has nothing to do with why the mentally ill can see through Obfuscate since, you know, they don't have superior senses.<br /> <br /> <br /> Because Obfuscate works by making observers ignore the sensory information they are receiving. It doesn't matter if you're receiving more detailed sensory information, Obfuscate still makes you ignore it. The vampire calling attention to itself breaks Obfuscate because if you're paying attention to the vampire you're not ignoring it any more. Also, stepping loudly is not an example of calling attention to yourself. The example is pulling a gun in a crowded place.<br /> <br /> <br /> Right, nothing. Extrasensory perception is not the reason animals can see through Obfuscate in The Blood (which, again, was demonstrably wrong in several places, even in 1e). It says that animals (and mentally ill people) can see through it not because their senses are more powerful, but because their brains are too simple for Obfuscate to fool. Extrasensory perception allows you to pierce Obfuscate because you're perceiving the vampire with something other than the 5 senses, something that Obfuscate doesn't make you ignore. Two completely separate things.<br /> <br /> And, if all this still doesn't convince you, Requiem 2e pretty directly states that Obfuscate works on werewolves.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not contending if it works or not, because it does. I'm arguing they can contest it with no additional gifts, because of a combination of super sensory perception, extra (spiritual) inbuilt perception, and animalistic instincts. Or just Primal Urge to summarize.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-29T08:49:47-08:00","id":839215,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/838159-werewolves-and-obfuscate?p=839202#post839202\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm not contending if it works or not, because it does. I'm arguing they can contest it with no additional gifts, because of a combination of super sensory perception, extra (spiritual) inbuilt perception, and animalistic instincts. Or just Primal Urge to summarize.</div> </div> </div> </div>Enhanced sensory perception doesn't pierce Obfuscate. Vampires have naturally enhanced sensory perception built into the template too, and can further improve it with a Merit, and neither of these things pierce Obfuscate. The only inbuilt extrasensory perception werewolves have is spirit senses. Which, granted, are about as extrasensory as it gets, but they perceive the other side of the gauntlet. If there's an obfuscated vampire in the <i>Hisil</i> when you turn on spirit senses, sure, go ahead and roll a Clash of Wills, but if it's in the flesh you're not even looking in the right dimensional plane to find it. Animalistic instincts, again, don't have anything to do with why The Blood said animals can see through Obfuscate. Mentally ill people don't have animalistic instincts but they can see through Obfuscate in The Blood too. The Blood is 1e anyway, and even in 1e The Blood was a dubious source. And lots of vampires have animalistic instincts too, especially Gangrel, but they can't Clash of Wills against Obfuscate without Auspex.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-29T09:02:01-08:00","id":839225,"title":"","content":"I think it should be clear by now no one's going to go back on their statement.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-01T02:31:07-08:00","id":839764,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/838159-werewolves-and-obfuscate?p=839158#post839158\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, since Obscufate is a mind hack power, the first dot anyways, wouldn't that mean stuff like Fearless Hunter might Clash it? Granted, the rules don't directly cause cause the Werewolf to sense since it's a &quot;defense&quot; against mental intrusions, but it's the idea being is that you're using a means to &quot;clear your mind&quot; of the psychic influence of the Vampire's obscufate, even though technically, that's not what the gift's fluff says.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd certainly allow it. The Gift protects from exactly the sort of mind-influencing powers that would weaken a hunter, like one that could force the werewolf to overlook her prey. It's exactly what the Clash of Wills rule was designed to do.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/838159-werewolves-and-obfuscate?p=838663#post838663\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would a werewolf in Kuruth, then, be able to target vampires in Obfuscation as if they weren't using it at all?</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a bit trickier. Werewolves are highly resistant to any such mind-influencing powers while Death Raging, so if nothing else you could allow a Clash of Wills, applying the normal penalty <i>Kuruth </i>inflicts to the vampire's roll. Otherwise, go with what makes for a better scene.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Freelancer </b>\u2022 Available for work!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","name":"Claire Redfield","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar109_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-01T05:14:26-08:00","id":839813,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Claire Redfield</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/838159-werewolves-and-obfuscate?p=839764#post839764\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'd certainly allow it. The Gift protects from exactly the sort of mind-influencing powers that would weaken a hunter, like one that could force the werewolf to overlook her prey. It's exactly what the Clash of Wills rule was designed to do.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> This is a bit trickier. Werewolves are highly resistant to any such mind-influencing powers while Death Raging, so if nothing else you could allow a Clash of Wills, applying the normal penalty <i>Kuruth </i>inflicts to the vampire's roll. Otherwise, go with what makes for a better scene.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hm. Does that mean Fearless Hunters secondary effects work too? The one where it also snaps the other pack members free from the enchantment?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-01T07:43:05-08:00","id":839890,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/838159-werewolves-and-obfuscate?p=839813#post839813\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hm. Does that mean Fearless Hunters secondary effects work too? The one where it also snaps the other pack members free from the enchantment?</div> </div> </div> </div>Why wouldn't it? Your pack follows your example, and Uratha hunt in packs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-01T08:09:20-08:00","id":839912,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/838159-werewolves-and-obfuscate?p=839890#post839890\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Why wouldn't it? Your pack follows your example, and Uratha hunt in packs.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Just confirming RAW since it never said anything about Clash of Wills.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-01T22:21:06-08:00","id":840412,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/838159-werewolves-and-obfuscate?p=839912#post839912\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just confirming RAW since it never said anything about Clash of Wills.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would say so, but I can't guarantee it. I'm just a freelancer, and didn't create all the rules for either <b>Vampire </b>or <b>Werewolf</b>. So it's not exactly RAW, and unless I get to be a Werewolf developer some day (one could only hope!), I have no authority to make it as such. I just speak to what I prefer in a game and go from there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Freelancer </b>\u2022 Available for work!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","name":"Claire Redfield","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar109_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-01T22:23:26-08:00","id":840413,"title":"","content":"I'd argue there really isn't a RAW here. As is usually the case with crossover interactons, there aren't a lot of rules written on it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-01T22:59:56-08:00","id":840428,"title":"","content":"Here's a bit from Beast about Clash of Wills.<br /> &quot;Sometimes, two supernatural powers clearly oppose one another. If the normal systems for the powers fail to resolve this, such as when two vampires attempt to Dominate the same person or a werewolf\u2019s heightened senses try to pierce a changeling\u2019s Contract of Smoke, use a Clash of Wills to decide the victor.\u2019&quot;<br /> <br /> In effect it could cause a Clash of Wills even if they dont call for it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10820-blakemikizuki","name":"Blakemikizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10820_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T10:50:23-08:00","id":840772,"title":"","content":"This example from the beast preview might help.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times\"><b><i>Example: </i></b><span style=\"font-family:Times\"><i>A werewolf, Kyle, and a Beast, Anika, have come into conflict. Kyle is attempting to</i><br /> <i>use Feet of Mist (the Gift of Cunning Evasion) to escape Anika. However, Anika has the Needs</i><br /> <i>Must Atavism, which hones her senses to preternatural levels and allows her to track damn near</i><br /> <i>anything, thus forcing the two characters enter a Clash of Wills. Kyle has three dots of Cunning</i><br /> <i>Renown and a Primal Urge of four, so his player will roll seven dice. Anika has five dots of Lair,</i><br /> <i>and her highest Resistance Attribute is her Composure of four dots, for a total of nine dice. Since</i><br /> <i>Anika has expended Satiety to invoke the most powerful effect of her Atavism, which allows her</i><br /> <i>to track a target indefinitely, her player adds four additional dice to her pool, for a total of</i><br /> <i>thirteen dice. Neither character can spend Willpower on the roll because Kyle isn</i><span style=\"font-family:Liberation Serif\"><i>\u2019</i><span style=\"font-family:Times\"><i>t on the scene,</i><br /> <i>and Anika has no way of knowing Kyle has masked his trail with spirit magic. Both players roll;</i><br /> <i>Kyle</i><span style=\"font-family:Liberation Serif\"><i>\u2019</i><span style=\"font-family:Times\"><i>s player gets three successes, while Anika</i><span style=\"font-family:Liberation Serif\"><i>\u2019</i><span style=\"font-family:Times\"><i>s rolls an impressive five. Anika</i><span style=\"font-family:Liberation Serif\"><i>\u2019</i><span style=\"font-family:Times\"><i>s Predatory</i><br /> <i>Awareness thus wins out over Kyle</i><span style=\"font-family:Liberation Serif\"><i>\u2019</i><span style=\"font-family:Times\"><i>s Feet of Mist, and Anika can track Kyle normally. To all</i><br /> <i>other characters, Kyle</i><span style=\"font-family:Liberation Serif\"><i>\u2019</i><span style=\"font-family:Times\"><i>s trail remains imperceptible.</i></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3323-cmwatford","name":"cmwatford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3323_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"192"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T10:54:23-08:00","id":840777,"title":"","content":"Someone tell those guys that Feet of Mist gets a rote action on Clash of Will rolls against attempts to detect them with supernatural powers.<br /> <br /> Even in the previews beast are OP!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T10:56:49-08:00","id":840779,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amravanti</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/838159-werewolves-and-obfuscate?p=840777#post840777\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Someone tell those guys that Feet of Mist gets a rote action on Clash of Will rolls against attempts to detect them with supernatural powers.<br /> <br /> Even in the previews beast are OP!</div> </div> </div> </div>I think Kyle just had a bad roll.<br /> <br /> <br /> It didn't say rerolls were counted or not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T11:07:20-08:00","id":840786,"title":"","content":"That's a slightly unfortunate example since it misses out a key element of Feet of Mist (the werewolf gets the Rote quality on that Clash of Wills) and is also a bit misleading re the Needs Must Atavism (it sort of works as indicated *if* the beast has marked the werewolf previously, but it doesn't mention that bit for some reason - it doesn't do anything to help if the beast has just found the trail of the werewolf but never marked them, since Needs Must's normal mode explicitly does nothing against magical obfuscations etc).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T11:18:51-08:00","id":840791,"title":"","content":"I really don't understand why people keep claiming that Beast is so overpowered. To my eye, they look like one of the weaker splats when it comes to acomplishing things, to be honest. Specifically in the fields of Combat, Investigation, Reasearch, Social Maneuvering, Chases, Crafting, hunting, socio-political-organization-fu, etc. Sure, they're better than mortals, but I generally put my money on other supernaturals in any of the above fields.<br /> <br /> Anyways, on subject. To answer the opening poster's question, my rule of thumb is that a passive ability generally cannot beat an activated power that you purchased with XP. In short:<br /> Active supernatural power &gt; passive supernatural power &gt; active innate ability &gt; passive innate ability<br /> <br /> So, a mage's passive Mage Sight won't work at noticing a Gift used to hide. No contest at all. You'd need some activated ability, and even then, Clash of Wills. So, in the case of an Uratha versus Kindred? Actively using some kind of sensory Gift to notice a vampire under Obfuscate. A werewolf using Impossible Spoor that was actively tracking the vampire? Clash of Wills as normal. A werewolf trying to track a vampire without such a Gift? Nope, auto failure. A werewolf with a Gift that gives passive Perception bonuses and not actively searching for something? No. Likewise, even if a werewolf is covered in blood, I would require Auspex to detect the werewolf if they're using a hiding Gift, despite smelling blood being an supernatural ability of supernaturally heightened Kindred senses. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T11:45:01-08:00","id":840805,"title":"","content":"I dunno, Beasts are pretty powerful but it depends entirely on the kit of the character in question. You can't really make judgements for them as a whole because their talents are even more reliant on individual qualities than the majority of splats, so they can seem like one of the less effective groups at accomplishing those things. As a whole they may be, but that's only because their inclinations are so scattered. There are a lot of terrifying tools in their loadout. Though I don't think they're overpowered (even if I stand by the thought that inter-splat balance is, if not a lie, then a low priority narratively and mechanically).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":188,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","user":"YeOfLittleFaith","date":". 03-02-2016, 04:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T11:57:16-08:00","id":840813,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/838159-werewolves-and-obfuscate?p=840791#post840791\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really don't understand why people keep claiming that Beast is so overpowered. To my eye, they look like one of the weaker splats when it comes to acomplishing things, to be honest. Specifically in the fields of Combat, Investigation, Reasearch, Social Maneuvering, Chases, Crafting, hunting, socio-political-organization-fu, etc. Sure, they're better than mortals, but I generally put my money on other supernaturals in any of the above fields.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was joking mostly, but I don't know how you think Beasts are not amazing at all of those.<br /> <br /> You just had the hunting example in the preview. There's Alien Allure for Social Maneuvering. Eye of Heaven and Mimir's Wisdom for Investigation/Research (+Advanced Library though thankfully that one is open to anyone). Wings of the Raptor for Chasing. <br /> <br /> And a half dozen combat atavisms that put most combat abilities to shame.<br /> <br /> And I haven't even touched on Nightmares. Maybe organization is their one weakness, but then they can just insert themselves into a pack or coterie or cabal and reap those benefits.<br /> <br /> Seriously read Mimir's Wisdom. It's easily the best Investigation tool among any splat barring maybe Mage.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T12:30:54-08:00","id":840844,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/838159-werewolves-and-obfuscate?p=840791#post840791\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really don't understand why people keep claiming that Beast is so overpowered. To my eye, they look like one of the weaker splats when it comes to acomplishing things, to be honest. Specifically in the fields of Combat, Investigation, Reasearch, Social Maneuvering, Chases, Crafting, hunting, socio-political-organization-fu, etc. Sure, they're better than mortals, but I generally put my money on other supernaturals in any of the above fields.</div> </div> </div> </div>They aren't OP on combat? Go reference half the atavisms. On investigation and research? Mimir's Well. Eye from Heaven. Social Maneuvering? Siren's Call. Chases? The one that let them merge with shadows and appear anywhere, at not cost. The rest is basically sub-system of the other.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T12:44:07-08:00","id":840852,"title":"","content":"My appologies to the thread.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amravanti</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/838159-werewolves-and-obfuscate?p=840813#post840813\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I was joking mostly, but I don't know how you think Beasts are not amazing at all of those.</div> </div> </div> </div> Simple really. All the powers you mention have very significant restrictions on their usage. Lets say we have a vamp, wolf, mage, 'ling, and beast all living together for some reason. Someone murders their neighbor.<br /> <br /> The vampire has access to Auspex and a couple rituals that allow tracking. The mage can do almost any of it depending on the Arcana. The werewolf can sniff out the killer immediately. The changeling, I imagine, can arrange a goblin vow.<br /> <br /> A Beast? Their tracking abilities rely on either 1) resonating with their Hunger, or 2) marking a target. And, even in the case of the Hunger, Needs Must doesn't track the killer specifically, only general instances that can feed one's Hunger in the immediate fascility - if the killer is long gone, there's no option. Epic Direction Sense is the only ability that's worth anything here, and pretty much everyone can do that too. Beast are the most worthless supernaturals at tracking out of the five examples because of these hard restrictions.<br /> <br /> Alien Allure gives lots of dice bonus. But given Social Maneuvering rules, you don't care about large dice pools outside of Forcing Doors/Hard Leverage. You care about Impressions and auto-opening Doors. Vampires bypass the need for doors entirely with Majesty/Dominate, and the vinculum gives Perfect impression. Mages have plenty of abilities, I'm sure. Same with Changelings; hells, feeding on emotions alone can be an advantage, since the target is weaker at resisting you now. Werewolves have some pretty potent abilities with Cunning and Purity Dominate. Beasts are pretty only good at Hard Leverage/Forcing Doors, and kinda sucky at the rest. Even the Obey Me! Nightmare is kinda weak since a mortal just obeys out of fear, and will split if given the option - its only an Integrity check, and you really can't force someone to make other Integrity checks with it - good chance your victim will run away first than obey you than get a worse breaking point.<br /> <br /> Wings of the Raptor only increases your speed for a few turns, and at a high cost; Urhan can actually chase down WotR like it was nothing using the current system. Changelings are the ultimate in evading pursuit by Hedge jumping. Mages have the option to teleport, as do the Khaibit.<br /> <br /> I've done white room comparisons between a combat Giant, a Rahu, and a Daeva. Generally speaking, the Rahu and Daeva came out ahead in terms of raw power. That's not even using the one insta-death merit Uratha get either. Demons I didn't even bother going all out - they decimate the opposition with Demon Form abilities and embeds that laugh off damage, not even Going Loud. There are embeds that paralize and kill people just with a look. In this case, its primarily because Vamp, Wolf, and Demon all come with innate abilities that are applicable for combat - Beasts have no innate combat abilities, only Atavisms or spell-like Nightmares.<br /> <br /> Mirmir's Wisdom is not better than simple divination rituals you can find in Vampire or Werewolf due to a very important restiction no one else has - it can't identify people. Auspex and Werewolf Gifts can easily do all the rest of Mirmir's normal effects. Low Satiety is primarily a social effect (granting Leverage), and again only related to one's Hunger. Satiety expendature gives you access to a library. Most supernaturals just have an actual library. Best investigative tool? I'm seriously wondering how its not in competition for the <i>worst</i>. Its mostly reproducing mundane talents or something a Mehket could easily pull off. I don't even want to think how much Knoweldge Gifts and Arcana put it to shame.<br /> <br /> For every Atavism or Nightmare, pretty much every game has a better and more effective alternative that's not burdened with the very specific identification problem that Beast suffers. As far as I can honestly tell, people are overreacting to the high power level of 2e as a whole, and mentally comparing Beasts to 1e games. The only advantage Beasts have over any other game is being extremely XP efficent. So, they grow in power faster than anyone else, but, as starting characters? They're by far the weakest and worst at a wide variety of things. Futhermore, the XP efficency is really only good at making combat monsters, of which I didn't include in my list.<br /> <br /> <br /> And most of these restrictions are by design. Beasts are <i>meant</i> to have trouble at Social Maneuvering outside of Forcing Doors/Hard Leverage. Social Maneuvering is how you make Kin. And, for a Beast, Kin are both power and survival. Beasts don't play nicely. They <i>take</i>. They're offensive. They appeal to the worst in all of us, the worst in the supernaturals. And that's how they make enemies through crossover actions. When it comes to tracking or investigation, their powers are hyper focused on whatever appeals to their Hungers. Anything outside the purview of their Hunger gets little to no love, so we're stuck with a hyper focus on filling out your Hunger in some way. Anyone else can do good with tracking abilities - Beasts have a hard time doing so. Beasts have less organization than even Werewolves, and no abilities that manipulate social merits like every other splat; this is deliberate, because they don't care about humans. <br /> <br /> Even with a specialized, made-to-order-Beast, there are just too many holes in their abilities to make them what I consider good at these things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 03-02-2016, 04:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T12:45:58-08:00","id":840855,"title":"","content":"I wholeheartedly disagree with literally every statement you've made, but I'd rather not turn this thread into yet another whiteroomer so we'll just agree to disagree on this one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-04T02:33:27-08:00","id":841793,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amravanti</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/838159-werewolves-and-obfuscate?p=840855#post840855\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wholeheartedly disagree with literally every statement you've made, but I'd rather not turn this thread into yet another whiteroomer so we'll just agree to disagree on this one.</div> </div> </div> </div>Aw, I was really hoping you would. I don't know jack about Beast and would have liked to see a rundown of how they stacked up to everyone else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-04T03:41:35-08:00","id":841808,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/838159-werewolves-and-obfuscate?p=840791#post840791\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, a mage's passive Mage Sight won't work at noticing a Gift used to hide. No contest at all. You'd need some activated ability, and even then, Clash of Wills.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yup. Peripheral Mage Sight won't notice it at all. Active Mage Sight would be a Clash of Wills, though as it's a Gift Active <i>Spirit</i> Mage Sight would give the mage's Clash of Wills the rote quality, too. Which would be one of the few cases of both sides in a contested roll both having Rote.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-04T04:19:43-08:00","id":841812,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amravanti</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/838159-werewolves-and-obfuscate?p=840855#post840855\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wholeheartedly disagree with literally every statement you've made, but I'd rather not turn this thread into yet another whiteroomer so we'll just agree to disagree on this one.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm with MCN on this. The power of most Beast abilities tends to get overstated to an extreme degree. Alien Allure probably being the worst offender, as it's actually really not that great.<br /> But agreed, let's keep that discussion away from this Werewolf thread.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=1109906#post1109906\" target=\"_blank\">My custom legacy</a> (2e)- The Disciples of Rathma - Life/Death focused Moros/Thyrsus Legacy, comments appreciated","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/166-joker","name":"Joker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"477"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}